<!-- Nov 1, 2009. Note on interpretation of pAWAntara entries (ejf note)
  a. It is the case that each instance of a <pAWAntara> element has as a child
     at least one <entry> element.
  b. In some cases (e.g., sutra 1.76), the pAWAntara <entry> element may be
     incomplete (or even empty).  In such cases, the missing <entry> 
     elements or attributes may be inferred from those of the non-pAWAntara
     entrie(s). For instance, in the case of 1.76, the preds attribute,
     the fullDAtu and lemma elements of the pAWAntara entry are inferred from
     the non-pAWAntara entry;  the sense element present in
     the pAWAntara element is to be used for the sense of the pAWAntara entry.
-->
